const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"代币价格与用户采用互相影响",en:"Token value and adoption interact"},body:{zh:"Cong、Li与Wang研究作为平台支付媒介的代币：更多用户可能提高平台交易价值，而预期代币升值又可能改变用户现在是否加入。它把采用决策与代币价格放在同一个动态模型里，不把用户数量简单当作外生估值倍数。",en:"Cong, Li and Wang model tokens used as platform payment media. More users can raise transaction utility, while expected token appreciation can affect today's participation. Adoption and valuation are jointly determined rather than treating user count as an external valuation multiple."}},{title:{zh:"理论对象，不是币价样本",en:"A theoretical economy, not a price sample"},body:{zh:"模型中的用户有不同交易需求，平台生产率随机变化，代币供给在基准设定中固定。用户决定是否承担参与成本，以及持有多少支付余额。文中提到具体平台是帮助解释机制，不是对这些币做出的样本回归或价格目标。",en:"Users differ in transaction needs, platform productivity is stochastic and baseline token supply is fixed. Agents choose participation and payment balances. Named platforms illustrate the mechanism; they are not an empirical price-regression sample or valuation targets."},reference:{url:"https://nengwang-economics.com/publications/papers/Cong_Li_Wang_RFS_2020_authorcopy.pdf",label:{zh:"作者版本第1节：平台经济模型",en:"Author copy §1: platform-economy model"}}},{title:{zh:"持有成本是关键连接",en:"Carrying cost connects the decisions"},body:{zh:"持有支付媒介意味着放弃其他资产的回报。在模型中，预期代币升值可以抵消部分机会成本，鼓励更早采用；用户增长又增加代币需求。这个反馈需要平台交易效用、网络效应与预期共同成立，不是仅靠限制发行数量就能推出价格上涨。",en:"Payment balances forgo returns on other assets. Expected token appreciation can offset part of that opportunity cost and encourage earlier adoption, while user growth increases demand. The feedback depends on transaction utility, network effects and expectations—not scarcity alone."}},{title:{zh:"模型给出的条件性结论",en:"Conditional model implications"},body:{zh:"作者描述了S形采用路径，以及在相同生产率过程下，代币平台相较无代币平台更快、更稳定的采用。网络效应也可能放大生产率冲击对价格的影响。因此，“采用更稳定”与“价格更稳定”不能混为一谈，更不能据此断言现实项目必然成功。",en:"The model produces S-shaped adoption and, relative to a tokenless platform with the same productivity process, accelerated and more stable participation. Network effects can also amplify price responses to productivity shocks. Stable adoption and stable prices are different claims."}},{title:{zh:"阅读时对照两种平台",en:"Compare like-for-like platforms"},body:{zh:"建议先读第1节，列出用户效用、参与成本、供给与贴现假设；随后比较有代币与使用普通计价商品的平台。尤其注意代币的权利：本文交易媒介并不等同于代表发行人现金流的证券型代币。用不同权利的资产替代，会改变模型问题。",en:"Start with utility, participation cost, supply and discounting assumptions in Section 1, then compare token and numeraire-settled platforms. Rights matter: transaction tokens here are distinct from claims on issuer cash flows. Substituting a different asset changes the model's question."},reference:{url:"https://nengwang-economics.com/publications/papers/Cong_Li_Wang_RFS_2020_authorcopy.pdf",label:{zh:"作者版本引言：代币范围与比较思路",en:"Author-copy introduction: token scope and comparison"}}},{title:{zh:"怎样准备后续观察材料",en:"Preparing subsequent observations"},body:{zh:"编辑建议：如果要研究现实平台，应分别定义真实用户、交易用途、代币余额和供给变更，并检查激励活动或机器人是否扭曲计数。交易所价格与成交量只能描述交易活动，不能替代平台采用和效用；本导读不输出估值、收益预测或买卖建议。",en:"Editorial application: define users, transaction uses, balances and supply changes separately, checking incentive-driven or automated activity. Exchange prices and volumes cannot substitute for platform adoption or utility. This guide produces no valuation, return forecast or trading recommendation."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2020年作者版本；书目保留2021年正式发表身份。理论比较不等于对现实代币的实证验证。",en:"The guide uses the 2020 author copy while retaining the 2021 publication identity. Theoretical comparisons are not empirical validation of live tokens."}};export{e as default};
